# Build context exclusions — keep the image build small and secret-free.
node_modules
.next
.git
.gitignore
.dockerignore
Dockerfile
docker-compose.yml
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
coverage
*.log
npm-debug.log*
.vscode
.idea
.DS_Store
*.tsbuildinfo
README.md
# Everything under data/ is personal and must never be baked into an image: the live
# profile, the training plans, and the lab documents a person uploads (data/lab/*.pdf).
# Nothing in it is tracked by git or needed to build; the container reads it from the
# ./data bind mount at run time instead. (A build from a git checkout, as CI does, never
# sees it; a build from a working folder, as `docker compose build` does, would.)
data
